From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caskade <caskade@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:05:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Scroll a wheel's notches further, and smoothly

A notch of a mouse wheel (a line delta) scrolled 20 px and jumped there.
It now scrolls Chromium's distance (100 px a line; 40 px on macOS, whose
line deltas are accelerated fractions) and glides there over 150 ms,
easing out, unless the user prefers reduced motion. Notches arriving
while it moves add to where it is heading. The first scroller along the
chain that can move takes the step; text inputs and sub-documents
scroll at once as before. Pixel deltas (touchpads) are unchanged.

Animated scrolls (these, smooth scrollTo and flings) used to move
without dispatching scroll events, so a virtual list never heard them.
The shell now sends a UiEvent::ScrollAnimationFrame before resolving
each frame while one runs; the event driver advances the animation
with resolve_scroll_animation_with and dispatches its scroll events.
